WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.117 --> 00:00:10.877
Brooklyn stared at her phone in shock. Who had sent her this mean text? Girls can't coach. Especially oafs like u.

2
00:00:10.879 --> 00:00:16.616
A player who hated her, obviously. She glanced uneasily around the gym.

3
00:00:16.617 --> 00:00:27.706
It was empty, except for two janitors, who were sweeping, and Marv, who was locking up the equipment closet.

4
00:00:27.707 --> 00:00:35.602
Brooklyn pulled back her shoulders. An elementary school teacher had once taught Brooklyn's class how to handle bullies.

5
00:00:35.603 --> 00:00:40.435
One thing Brooklyn remembered was to never let bullies bother you.

6
00:00:40.436 --> 00:00:45.098
And if they did bother you, you were supposed to talk to an adult about it.

7
00:00:45.099 --> 00:00:53.002
"Take that!" Brooklyn pressed Delete on her phone. She instantly felt better.

8
00:00:53.003 --> 00:01:02.736
But at school on Monday, Brooklyn found a note folded up inside her locker: You're no coach!

9
00:01:02.737 --> 00:01:12.975
On Tuesday there was another note in her lunch bag: We need a real coach. Not you. On

10
00:01:12.976 --> 00:01:21.326
Wednesday she found one in her gym bag: Leave the Whales. On

11
00:01:21.327 --> 00:01:29.223
Thursday a note lay inside her history book: Quit or the team will lose. Brooklyn

12
00:01:29.224 --> 00:01:39.235
kept the messages to herself. But on Friday she pulled Jacey aside before math class. She

13
00:01:39.236 --> 00:01:47.385
showed her the latest note, found in her backpack that morning: Oafs don't coach. Jacey's

14
00:01:47.386 --> 00:01:51.699
eyes widened. "That's so mean." "It's

15
00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:58.451
not the first message I've gotten this week." Brooklyn told her friend about the other messages. "Have

16
00:01:58.452 --> 00:02:01.773
you told anyone?" Jacey asked. Brooklyn

17
00:02:01.774 --> 00:02:03.571
shook her head. "The

18
00:02:03.572 --> 00:02:10.949
final game is coming up, so I didn't want to get anyone in trouble. Do you think Dirk wrote these notes?" Jacey

19
00:02:10.950 --> 00:02:15.954
shrugged. "I know Dirk was mad about being benched." "That

20
00:02:15.955 --> 00:02:24.918
was his fault, not mine," Brooklyn said as the bell rang. "We'll talk more at practice," she said quickly. But

21
