Brooklyn didn't get a chance to talk to Jacey at practice. Instead

22
00:02:28.831 --> 00:02:36.672
she spent almost the entire session walking around school searching for Dirk. Someone

23
00:02:36.673 --> 00:02:43.251
said they saw him in the office, so she checked there. No Dirk. Someone

24
00:02:43.252 --> 00:02:48.326
else claimed he was in the library. No Dirk. This

25
00:02:48.327 --> 00:02:52.652
was their last practice before the play-off game on Saturday. While

26
00:02:52.653 --> 00:03:02.323
Marv led the team through the loop play, Brooklyn used the phone in the gym office. She

27
00:03:02.324 --> 00:03:09.457
called Dirk's cell phone and his home, but no one answered either number. When

28
00:03:09.458 --> 00:03:17.552
Brooklyn went to tell Marv the news, she heard Jacey laughing out in the hall at the water fountain. "She

29
00:03:17.553 --> 00:03:20.834
wants to be a professional coach!" "Really?"

30
00:03:20.835 --> 00:03:24.471
Stuart laughed. "Can

31
00:03:24.472 --> 00:03:28.292
you coach if you don't even play?" Aaron asked. "Brooklyn wants

32
00:03:28.293 --> 00:03:34.220
to," said Jacey. "It's her big dream." Brooklyn hurried

33
00:03:34.221 --> 00:03:44.438
away before they spotted her. "I can't believe Jacey told them about my dream of coaching," she thought. Tears stung

34
00:03:44.439 --> 00:03:51.953
her eyes. It was the truth, but the way Jacey had said it made Brooklyn feel silly. Were Aaron

35
00:03:51.954 --> 00:03:58.366
and Stuart laughing at her? She blinked quickly to keep her tears from spilling. Outside the

36
00:03:58.367 --> 00:04:11.261
gym Brooklyn took a few deep breaths. She had to calm down. The team

37
00:04:11.262 --> 00:04:17.672
had had a great season. And if things went well, they could be league champions. She squared

38
00:04:17.673 --> 00:04:27.312
her shoulders and stepped onto the basketball court next to Marv. "What's next, Coach?" * *

39
00:04:27.313 --> 00:04:31.907
* After practice Brooklyn put away the

40
00:04:31.908 --> 00:04:37.144
equipment. Marv looked at her. "You were awfully quiet today," he

41
00:04:37.145 --> 00:04:42.567
said. "I was worried about . . . um, the final game. And

42
00:04:42.568 --> 00:04:48.131
Dirk." "We'll be fine," Marv said grimly. "With or without

43
00:04:48.132 --> 00:04:56.047
Dirk." When Brooklyn reached her house thirty minutes later, she was surprised to see Dirk sitting on her front steps holding a

44
00:04:56.048 --> 00:05:02.372
basketball. "Where were you?" Brooklyn demanded. "Today's final practice was super

45
00:05:02.373 --> 00:05:07.543
important." "I went to talk to Coach Teagan," Dirk said. "About the

46
00:05:07.544 --> 00:05:11.218
team. And after talking to you, I'm going to talk to

47
00:05:11.219 --> 00:05:19.532
Marv." Dirk took a big breath. "I didn't like you giving us plays, but you do seem to know your

48
00:05:19.533 --> 00:05:24.347
stuff. I know I haven't been a team player, and I'm

49
00:05:24.348 --> 00:05:30.670
sorry." Brooklyn was proud to hear Dirk say she knew her stuff with basketball. "It's okay," she

50
00:05:30.671 --> 00:05:35.858
said. "Thanks. And don't worry. I didn't let those notes bother

51
00:05:35.859 --> 00:05:39.320
me." Dirk frowned, confused. "What notes?"

52
00:05:39.321 --> 00:05:45.835
Brooklyn studied his face. "You didn't leave mean notes for me? Or text me?"

53
00:05:45.836 --> 00:05:51.747
Dirk shook his head. "That's creepy, Brooklyn. I'd never do something like that."

54
00:05:51.748 --> 00:05:55.490
"If it wasn't you . . . ," Brooklyn began.

55
00:05:55.491 --> 00:05:58.675
"What do the notes say?" Dirk asked.

56
00:05:58.676 --> 00:06:05.904
"Uh . . . never mind," she said quickly. She was still worried about upsetting the team before the final game.

57
00:06:05.905 --> 00:06:12.745
"Anyway, Marv said you'll have to sit out for the first quarter of tomorrow's game because you missed practice.

58
00:06:12.746 --> 00:06:16.742
